<style>
/* Layout: the RxC results template, in the Warringah brand: a cyan hero and closing band with navy type,
   white sections, a navy band for the uncommon ground. Two group colours of equal weight (gold, violet),
   neither of them the brand's cyan or navy. */
:root{
  --cyan:#00b4cd; --on-cyan:#13384b; --navy:#13384b;
  --g1:#a97c0c; --g2:#7562d4; --g1-soft:#f6f0e1; --g2-soft:#efedfb;
  --paper:#ffffff; --ink:#212529; --heading:#13384b; --card:#ffffff; --muted:#56606a;
  --line:rgba(19,56,75,.16); --track:#e2e8eb; --tint:#e6f6f9; --deep:#13384b;
  --display:"Poppins","Century Gothic","Avenir Next",system-ui,sans-serif;
  --text:"Inter",system-ui,-apple-system,"Segoe UI",Arial,sans-serif;
  color-scheme:light;
  box-sizing:border-box;
  padding-top:env(safe-area-inset-top,0px);
  padding-bottom:env(safe-area-inset-bottom,0px);
}
@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){
  :root:not([data-theme="light"]){
    --g1:#bb8b1a; --g2:#8d7ce6; --g1-soft:#272212; --g2-soft:#1e1c36;
    --paper:#0e1b22; --ink:#e7eef1; --heading:#e7eef1; --card:#132630; --muted:#a9b8c0;
    --line:rgba(255,255,255,.15); --track:#2a3d47; --tint:#0f2b34; --deep:#0a1820; color-scheme:dark;
  }
}
:root[data-theme="dark"]{
  --g1:#bb8b1a; --g2:#8d7ce6; --g1-soft:#272212; --g2-soft:#1e1c36;
  --paper:#0e1b22; --ink:#e7eef1; --heading:#e7eef1; --card:#132630; --muted:#a9b8c0;
  --line:rgba(255,255,255,.15); --track:#2a3d47; --tint:#0f2b34; --deep:#0a1820; color-scheme:dark;
}
*,*::before,*::after{box-sizing:inherit}
html{scroll-padding-top:env(safe-area-inset-top,0px);scroll-behavior:smooth;-webkit-text-size-adjust:100%}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){html{scroll-behavior:auto}}
body{margin:0;font-family:var(--text);color:var(--ink);background:var(--paper);font-size:18px;line-height:1.5;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased}
.wrap{max-width:77.5rem;margin:0 auto;padding:0 40px}
h1,h2,h3{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:700;margin:0;letter-spacing:-.015em;color:var(--heading)}
p{margin:0}
a{color:inherit}
:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--ink);outline-offset:3px}
.btn{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;padding:.9rem 1.45rem;border-radius:999px;font-weight:600;font-size:1.02rem;text-decoration:none;border:2px solid var(--navy);font-family:inherit;cursor:pointer}
.btn.solid{background:var(--navy);color:#fff}
.btn.line{background:transparent;color:var(--navy)}
.btn:hover{transform:translateY(-1px)}
.dot{width:12px;height:12px;border-radius:50%;display:inline-block;flex:none}
.dot.g1{background:var(--g1)} .dot.g2{background:var(--g2)}
.pill{display:inline-block;font-weight:600;font-size:.9rem;background:var(--navy);color:#fff;border-radius:99px;padding:.3rem .85rem}
q{quotes:"“" "”"}

/* ---------- hero ---------- */
.hero{background:var(--cyan);color:var(--on-cyan);overflow:hidden}
.hero h1{color:var(--on-cyan)}
.hero :focus-visible{outline-color:var(--navy)}
.hero-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.05fr 1fr;gap:48px;align-items:center;padding:80px 0 92px}
/* The headline is three set lines, the middle one boxed like the stepped headlines on the MP's site.
   Its longest line is 8.76em wide, so it is sized from its column (10.6cqi) and capped by the window height. */
.hero-text{container-type:inline-size;min-width:0}
.hero h1{font-size:min(10.6cqi,9vh,4.6rem);line-height:1.12;margin-bottom:28px}
.hero h1 .ln{display:block;white-space:nowrap}
.hero h1 .box{display:inline-block;background:var(--navy);color:#fff;padding:.02em .2em .1em;margin:.1em 0 .12em -.2em;border-radius:.07em;line-height:1.1}
.hero .sub{font-size:1.3rem;line-height:1.45;max-width:30rem;margin-bottom:32px}
.hero .turnout{font-size:.95rem;font-weight:500;margin-top:22px}
.actions{display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap}
.cards{position:relative;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:20px;padding-top:max(10px,calc(3.43rem - 56px))}
.card{position:relative;width:82%;background:#fff;color:var(--navy);border-radius:18px;padding:22px 26px;box-shadow:0 18px 40px -18px rgba(9,40,54,.5)}
.card q{display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:1.14rem;line-height:1.36}
.sticker{position:relative;width:8.25rem;height:8.25rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--navy);color:#fff;display:grid;place-items:center;text-align:center;transform:rotate(-12deg);z-index:3;padding:0 .7rem}
.sticker b{display:block;font-family:var(--display);font-weight:700;font-size:1.9rem;line-height:1;margin:.1rem 0 .2rem}
.sticker span{display:block;font-size:.6rem;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2}
/* Hero: two quote cards, one per group, with the circle between them (the results pages' common format,
   18 November 2026). The circle is relative, not absolute, so it stays above both cards where it overlaps them. */
.hero .sub{max-width:none}

.hero .card{overflow:hidden}
.hero .card::before{content:"";position:absolute;left:0;top:0;bottom:0;width:7px;background:var(--gc)}
.hero .card.c1{--gc:var(--g1)}
.hero .card.c2{--gc:var(--g2)}
.hero .card .who{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5em;margin:0 0 .55rem;font-size:.82rem;font-weight:700;line-height:1.25;letter-spacing:.01em}
.hero .card .who i{flex:none;width:.8em;height:.8em;border-radius:50%;background:var(--gc)}
/* The circle's ring is half Group 1's colour (top, towards card 1) and half Group 2's (bottom, towards card 2).
   "from -78deg" undoes the sticker's -12deg tilt so the split stays level. */
.hero .sticker{border:6px solid transparent;background:linear-gradient(var(--navy),var(--navy)) padding-box,conic-gradient(from -78deg,var(--g1) 0 50%,var(--g2) 0 100%) border-box}

/* Wide screens: the circle clasps both cards at the seam, on the right */
@media (min-width:901px){
  .hero .cards{gap:30px}
  .hero .card.c1{align-self:flex-start;width:calc(100% - 6rem);padding:26px 46px 30px 36px}
  .hero .card.c2{align-self:flex-start;margin-left:1.5rem;width:calc(100% - 7.5rem);padding:26px 46px 30px 36px}
  .hero .card q{font-size:1.32rem;line-height:1.38}
  .hero .sticker{position:relative;top:auto;right:auto;align-self:flex-end;margin:calc(-15px - 4.125rem) -14px calc(-15px - 4.125rem) 0}
}
/* Short laptop screens: a little smaller so both cards stay on the first screen */
@media (min-width:901px) and (max-height:53em){
  .hero .cards{gap:24px}
  .hero .card.c1,.hero .card.c2{padding:22px 44px 24px 32px}
  .hero .card q{font-size:1.2rem;line-height:1.36}
  .hero .sticker{margin:calc(-12px - 4.125rem) -14px calc(-12px - 4.125rem) 0}
}
/* Narrow laptops (two columns but a slim card column): full-width cards with the circle between them */
@media (min-width:901px) and (max-width:56.25em){
  .hero .card.c1,.hero .card.c2{width:auto;align-self:stretch;margin-left:0;padding:22px 26px 24px 30px}
  .hero .sticker{align-self:center;margin:-16px 0}
}
/* Phones: the same, under the hero text */
@media (max-width:900px){
  .hero .sticker{align-self:center;margin:-14px 0}
}
@media (min-width:901px){
  .hero-grid{padding-top:clamp(28px,calc(100vh - 41.5rem),80px)}
}
/* Short windows, or large text in a window that isn't tall: a smaller headline and lede keep the buttons
   on the first screen. 46em follows the reader's text size (736px at 16px, 920px at 20px). See the README. */
@media (min-width:901px) and (max-height:46em){
  .hero h1{font-size:min(10.6cqi,8vh,4.6rem);margin-bottom:20px}
  .hero .sub{font-size:1.12rem;margin-bottom:22px}
  .hero .turnout{margin-top:16px}
}
@media (min-width:901px) and (max-height:43.25em),(min-width:901px) and (max-width:62.5em) and (max-height:53em){
  .hero-grid{align-items:start}
}

/* ---------- sections ---------- */
section.block{padding:104px 0}
.head{margin-bottom:46px}
.head h2{font-size:clamp(2.1rem,3.6vw,3.3rem);line-height:1.08;max-width:22ch;text-wrap:balance}
.head p{font-size:1.2rem;line-height:1.45;max-width:36rem}
.head .head-line{margin-top:18px;max-width:42rem}
/* a heading with a lead: side by side on wide screens, so neither leaves half the width empty */
.head.side{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.05fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:20px 56px;align-items:end}
.head.side .head-line{margin-top:0}
.deep{background:var(--deep);color:#fff}
.deep h2{color:#fff}
.deep .head p{color:#d3e2e8}
.tint{background:var(--tint)}

/* ---------- at a glance ---------- */
.glance{padding:64px 0 0}
.glance-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:24px}
.gl{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px;border-radius:24px;padding:28px 28px 26px;text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);border:2px solid var(--navy);background:var(--card);transition:transform .15s ease}
.gl:hover{transform:translateY(-3px)}
.gl h3{font-size:1.45rem;line-height:1.15}
.gl p{font-size:1rem;line-height:1.45;flex:1}
.gl .more{font-weight:600;font-size:.95rem;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.2em}
.gl.dark{background:var(--navy);color:#fff;border-color:var(--navy)}
.gl.dark h3{color:var(--cyan)}
.gl.tinted{background:var(--tint)}
.split{display:flex;height:18px;border-radius:99px;overflow:hidden;gap:2px}
.split i{display:block;height:100%}
.split-n{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:.9rem;font-weight:600;margin-top:-6px}
.split-n span{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:7px}
@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){:root:not([data-theme="light"]) .gl{border-color:var(--line)}}
:root[data-theme="dark"] .gl{border-color:var(--line)}

/* ---------- group cards ---------- */
.groups-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:28px;margin-top:28px}
.gcard{border-radius:28px;padding:26px 30px 30px;background:var(--gsoft);border-top:12px solid var(--gc)}
.gcard.one{--gc:var(--g1);--gsoft:var(--g1-soft)} .gcard.two{--gc:var(--g2);--gsoft:var(--g2-soft)}
.gtop{display:flex;align-items:flex-end;gap:18px;margin-bottom:20px}
.gtop .big{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:700;font-size:3.6rem;line-height:.95;color:var(--heading);white-space:nowrap}
.gtop .big small{font-size:.5em;font-weight:600}
.gtop .who{font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.3;padding-bottom:6px}
.gtop .who b{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px;font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:700;font-family:var(--display);color:var(--heading)}
.gtop .who b .dot{width:14px;height:14px}
.qbox{background:var(--card);color:var(--ink);border-radius:18px;padding:18px 22px 18px;margin-top:12px}
.qbox q{display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:1.1rem;line-height:1.34;margin-bottom:12px}
.qbox.lead q{font-size:1.26rem}
.qbox .lab{font-size:.88rem;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:6px}
.pcts{display:flex;gap:8px 20px;font-size:.95rem;flex-wrap:wrap}
.pcts span{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px}
.pcts b{font-weight:600}
.small-note{font-size:.95rem;color:var(--muted);margin-top:22px;max-width:46rem}
.sub-head{margin:84px 0 26px}
.sub-head h3{font-size:clamp(1.7rem,2.6vw,2.4rem);line-height:1.12}

/* ---------- map: one row along the main divide ---------- */
.map-card{position:relative;border:2px solid var(--navy);border-radius:28px;padding:22px 26px 18px;background:var(--card)}
@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){:root:not([data-theme="light"]) .map-card{border-color:var(--line)}}
:root[data-theme="dark"] .map-card{border-color:var(--line)}
.map-lead{font-weight:600;font-size:1.05rem;margin-bottom:8px;max-width:46rem}
.map-foot{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:8px}
.map-legend{display:flex;gap:22px;flex-wrap:wrap;font-size:.98rem;font-weight:500}
.map-legend span{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px}
.someone{font:inherit;font-size:.95rem;font-weight:600;background:var(--navy);color:#fff;border:0;border-radius:99px;padding:.55rem 1.1rem;cursor:pointer}
@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){:root:not([data-theme="light"]) .someone{background:var(--ink);color:var(--paper)}}
:root[data-theme="dark"] .someone{background:var(--ink);color:var(--paper)}
#map{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;touch-action:manipulation;cursor:crosshair;overflow:visible}
#map .pdot{transition:transform 1.2s cubic-bezier(.2,.75,.2,1),fill .6s ease,opacity .6s ease}
#map .axis{stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:2}
#map .axis-label{fill:var(--ink);font-family:var(--text);font-weight:600}
.map-hint{font-size:.95rem;color:var(--muted);margin-top:6px}
.map-hint .h-touch{display:none}
@media (hover:none){.map-hint .h-fine{display:none}.map-hint .h-touch{display:inline}}
/* a closer look inside Group 2: one divider on the map, names over the two stretches, and a key */
#map .st-div{stroke:var(--ink);opacity:.4;pointer-events:none}
#map .st-name{fill:var(--ink);font-family:var(--text);font-weight:600}
#map .st-count{fill:var(--muted);font-family:var(--text)}
#map .st-badge{fill:var(--ink)}
#map .grp-name{fill:var(--ink);font-family:var(--text);font-weight:700}
#map .st-bracket{stroke:var(--ink);opacity:.45}
#map .st-num{fill:var(--card);font-family:var(--text);font-weight:700;pointer-events:none}
.st-key{border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin-top:16px;padding-top:16px}
.st-h{font-weight:600;font-size:1.02rem;line-height:1.4;margin-bottom:4px}
.st-list{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}
.st-list li{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,17.5rem) minmax(0,1fr);gap:4px 28px;align-items:baseline;padding:11px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.45}
.st-list li:last-child{border-bottom:0}
.st-list li.g2row{border-bottom:0;padding-bottom:2px}
/* Group 2's two parts sit under its heading, set in from a thin rule */
.st-list li.part{margin-left:.4rem;padding-left:1.1rem;border-left:2px solid var(--line);grid-template-columns:minmax(0,calc(17.5rem - 1.5rem - 2px)) minmax(0,1fr)}
.st-list li.part + li.part{border-top:0}
.st-t .dot{width:11px;height:11px}
.st-t{display:flex;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:4px 9px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.3}
.st-b{display:none;flex:none;place-items:center;width:22px;height:22px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ink);color:var(--card);font-size:.76rem;font-weight:700;line-height:1}
.st-c{font-weight:400;color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;white-space:nowrap}
.map-card.compact .st-b{display:inline-grid}
@media (max-width:700px){ .st-list li,.st-list li.part{grid-template-columns:1fr} }
.person{position:absolute;z-index:5;width:330px;background:var(--card);color:var(--ink);border:2px solid var(--ink);border-radius:18px;padding:16px 18px 14px;box-shadow:0 18px 40px -20px rgba(0,0,0,.5);font-size:.92rem;line-height:1.4;pointer-events:none;opacity:0;transform:translateY(4px);transition:opacity .15s ease,transform .15s ease}
.person.on{opacity:1;transform:none}
.person .pg{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;font-weight:600;font-size:1rem;margin-bottom:6px}
.person .pn{color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:10px}
.person .pn b{color:var(--ink);font-weight:600}
.person .lean-h{font-weight:600;font-size:.88rem;margin:12px 0 7px}
.lean{display:flex;height:12px;border-radius:99px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--track);gap:2px}
.lean i{display:block;height:100%}
.lean .l1{background:var(--g1)} .lean .l2{background:var(--g2)}
.lean-n{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:10px;font-size:.84rem;margin-top:6px}
.lean-n span{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px}
.lean-n b{font-weight:600}
.person .note{margin-top:10px;font-size:.88rem;line-height:1.4}
.person .ex{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:9px;margin-top:10px}
.person .ex .exl{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;font-size:.84rem;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:4px}
.person .ex q{display:block}

/* ---------- dumbbells ---------- */
.dumb{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;margin-top:14px;overflow:visible}
.dumb .trk{stroke:var(--trk,var(--track))}
.dumb .rng{stroke:var(--rng,var(--ink))}
.dumb .tick{fill:var(--tk,var(--muted));font-family:var(--text)}
.dumb .ring{stroke:var(--ring,var(--card))}
.vals{display:flex;gap:8px 22px;font-size:.98rem;margin-top:8px;flex-wrap:wrap}
.vals span{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px}
.vals b{font-weight:600}
.nn{color:var(--muted);font-weight:400;font-size:.88em}

/* ---------- pairs ---------- */
.pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;border-radius:28px;overflow:hidden;margin-bottom:28px;background:var(--card);color:var(--ink)}
.pair .topic{grid-column:1/-1;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;gap:1rem;padding:26px 34px 0}
.pair .topic h3{font-size:1.7rem;line-height:1.15}
.pair .topic .n{font-size:.9rem;color:var(--muted);white-space:nowrap}
.half{padding:22px 34px 30px}
.half.split-half{margin:18px 0}
.half.agree{background:var(--cyan);color:var(--navy);margin:18px 18px 18px 0;border-radius:20px;--trk:rgba(19,56,75,.22);--rng:var(--navy);--tk:var(--navy);--ring:var(--navy)}
.half.agree .nn{color:var(--navy)}
.half.agree .dot{box-shadow:0 0 0 1.5px var(--navy)}
.half q{display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:1.24rem;line-height:1.32;min-height:3.96em;margin-top:14px}
details.all{margin-top:8px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.3);padding-top:18px}
details.all summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600;font-size:1.05rem;padding:.2rem 0}
.all-list{list-style:none;margin:16px 0 0;padding:0;column-count:2;column-gap:44px}
.all-list li{break-inside:avoid;padding:12px 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.18)}
.all-list q{display:block;font-weight:500;line-height:1.4}
.all-list .vals{color:#d3e2e8;font-size:.9rem;margin-top:4px}

/* ---------- priorities ---------- */
.how{display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;gap:40px;align-items:center;background:var(--card);border:2px solid var(--navy);border-radius:24px;padding:26px 32px;margin-bottom:40px}
.costs{display:flex;gap:28px;align-items:flex-end}
.cost{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:10px;font-size:.92rem;text-align:center}
.cost b{font-weight:600}
.sq{display:grid;gap:3px}
.sq i{width:16px;height:16px;border-radius:3px;background:var(--cyan);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1.5px var(--navy)}
.sq.s1{grid-template-columns:repeat(1,16px)} .sq.s4{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,16px)} .sq.s9{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,16px)}
.how p.cap{font-size:1.1rem;line-height:1.45;max-width:36rem}
.finding{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:700;color:var(--heading);font-size:clamp(1.35rem,2.1vw,1.8rem);line-height:1.2;margin:0 0 26px;max-width:44rem}
.prio-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:24px}
.pcard{background:var(--card);border-radius:24px;padding:26px 26px 24px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;border:2px solid var(--navy)}
@supports (grid-template-rows:subgrid){.pcard{display:grid;grid-row:span 5;grid-template-rows:subgrid;row-gap:0}.pcard .echo{align-self:start}}
.pcard .rank{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:700;font-size:2.4rem;line-height:1;margin-bottom:12px;color:var(--heading)}
.pcard .tt{margin-bottom:22px;flex:1}
.pcard p.t{font-weight:600;font-size:1.12rem;line-height:1.32}
/* each change leads with its net votes, which set the order; one bar on a shared scale (the top change is full width) */
.tally{margin:0 0 12px}
.tally .big{display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:.45rem;margin:0 0 12px;font-family:var(--display);font-weight:700;font-size:2.7rem;line-height:1;color:var(--heading)}
.tally .big span{font-family:var(--text);font-size:.95rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--muted)}
.tbar{height:10px;border-radius:5px;background:var(--track);overflow:hidden}
.tbar i{display:block;height:100%;border-radius:5px;background:var(--cyan)}
.pstats{font-size:.95rem;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap}
.pstats b{font-weight:600}
.pcard .pstats{color:var(--muted);font-size:.92rem}
.echo{border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin-top:18px;padding-top:14px}
.echo .el{font-size:.85rem;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:6px}
.echo .en{font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted);margin-top:6px}
.echo q{display:block;font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.38;margin-bottom:4px}
.echo .vals{font-size:.9rem;margin-top:6px}
.no-card{margin-top:28px;background:var(--navy);color:#fff;border-radius:28px;padding:34px 38px;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:40px;align-items:center}
.no-card h3{font-size:2rem;line-height:1.1;margin:0 0 14px;color:var(--cyan)}
.no-card p.t{font-weight:600;font-size:1.28rem;line-height:1.32;margin-bottom:14px}
.no-card p.s{color:#d3e2e8;font-size:1rem}
.no-card .tally .big{color:#fff}
.no-card .tally .big span{color:#d3e2e8}
details.rest{margin-top:28px;border-top:2px solid var(--navy);padding-top:18px}
details.rest summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600;font-size:1.05rem;padding:.2rem 0}
.rest-list{list-style:none;margin:16px 0 0;padding:0}
.rest-list li{display:grid;grid-template-columns:3rem 1fr auto;gap:16px;align-items:baseline;padding:14px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
.rest-list .r{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:700;font-size:1.4rem;line-height:1;color:var(--heading)}
.rest-list .t{font-weight:600}
.rest-list .s{font-size:.92rem;color:var(--muted);white-space:nowrap;display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:.6rem}
.rest-list .rnet{font-family:var(--display);font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--heading)}
.rest-list .rs{font-size:.9rem}

/* ---------- how this worked ---------- */
.steps{list-style:none;margin:0 0 30px;padding:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:20px}
.step{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px;border:2px solid var(--navy);border-radius:24px;padding:24px 24px 26px;background:var(--card)}
.step .fig{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:700;font-size:2.6rem;line-height:1;color:var(--heading)}
.step h3{font-family:var(--text);font-weight:600;font-size:1.1rem;letter-spacing:0;line-height:1.3;margin-top:4px}
.step p{font-size:.98rem;line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}
@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){:root:not([data-theme="light"]) :is(.step,.how,.pcard){border-color:var(--line)}}
:root[data-theme="dark"] :is(.step,.how,.pcard){border-color:var(--line)}
details.fine{border-top:2px solid var(--navy);padding-top:18px}
details.fine summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600;font-size:1.05rem;padding:.2rem 0}
details.fine .arows{margin-top:14px}
.arows{border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
.arow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,2fr);column-gap:32px;padding:24px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
.arow > p{grid-column:2}
.arow h3{font-family:var(--text);font-weight:600;font-size:1.12rem;letter-spacing:0;line-height:1.35}
.arow p{font-size:1.02rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:44rem}
.arow p + p{margin-top:.6rem}

/* ---------- what happens next + footer ---------- */
.next{background:var(--cyan);color:var(--navy);padding:104px 0;position:relative;overflow:hidden}
.next h2{color:var(--navy);font-size:clamp(2.4rem,4.4vw,4rem);line-height:1.05;margin-bottom:24px}
.next-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,38rem) auto;justify-content:start;gap:48px 88px;align-items:center}
.next p{font-size:1.3rem;line-height:1.45;max-width:32rem;margin-bottom:32px}
.next .sticker2{justify-self:center;width:15rem;height:15rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--navy);color:#fff;display:grid;place-items:center;text-align:center;transform:rotate(-10deg);padding:1.2rem}
.next .sticker2 b{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:700;font-size:2.1rem;line-height:1.1;display:block}
footer{background:var(--navy);color:#fff;padding:48px 0 56px}
.foot{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:32px}
.foot strong{font-weight:600}
.foot .ack{color:#c8d8df;font-size:.95rem}

@media (max-width:900px){
  .wrap{padding:0 20px}
  .hero-grid,.head,.head.side,.groups-row,.pair,.no-card,.foot,.glance-grid,.sub-head,.next-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}
  .head.side .head-line{margin-top:18px}
  .sub-head{margin:64px 0 20px}
  .how{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:20px;padding:22px}
  .costs{gap:20px}
  .arow{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:6px;padding:18px 0}
  .arow > p{grid-column:auto}
  .steps{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:14px}
  .step{padding:20px}
  .step .fig{font-size:2.2rem}
  .next{padding:72px 0}
  .next .sticker2{width:10.625rem;height:10.625rem}
  .next .sticker2 b{font-size:1.5rem}
  .glance{padding:44px 0 0}
  .hero-grid{padding:28px 0 64px;gap:28px}
  .hero h1{font-size:min(10.6cqi,3rem)}
  .hero .sub{font-size:1.15rem}
  .cards{gap:16px;padding:6px 4px 10px}
  .card{width:auto;align-self:stretch}
  section.block{padding:72px 0}
  .head{gap:18px;margin-bottom:30px}
  .gtop .big{font-size:2.9rem}
  .gcard{padding:22px 20px 24px}
  .map-card{padding:16px 14px 14px;border-radius:22px}
  .person{position:static;width:auto;opacity:1;transform:none;margin-top:12px;box-shadow:none;display:none}
  .person.on{display:block}
  .half.agree{margin:0 14px 14px}
  .half.split-half{margin:6px 0 0}
  .pair .topic{padding:22px 22px 0;flex-wrap:wrap}
  .pair .topic h3{font-size:1.45rem}
  .half{padding:18px 22px 24px}
  .half q{min-height:0}
  .all-list{column-count:1}
  .prio-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}
  .no-card{padding:28px 22px;gap:22px}
  .rest-list li{grid-template-columns:2.4rem 1fr}
  .rest-list .s{grid-column:2;white-space:normal}
}
@media (hover:hover) and (pointer:fine){
  .pair,.pcard,.no-card{transition:opacity .2s ease}
  #pairs:has(.pair:hover) .pair:not(:hover),
  #priorities:has(.pcard:hover) .pcard:not(:hover),
  #priorities:has(.pcard:hover) .no-card,
  #priorities:has(.no-card:hover) .pcard{opacity:.25}
}
@media (hover:hover) and (pointer:fine) and (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){ .pair,.pcard,.no-card{transition:none} }
@media (max-width:520px){ .steps{grid-template-columns:1fr} }
@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){ #map .pdot,.person,.gl{transition:none} .btn:hover,.gl:hover{transform:none} }

/* ---------- RxC site shell (shared with the other project microsites) ---------- */
.rxc-shell{--ink:#17203A;--paper:#fff;--common:#EDFF38;--quiet:#5F657E;--hair:#D9DBE3;--voice-b:#E23A6B;
  font-family:"Bricolage Grotesque",system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--ink);background:var(--paper);font-size:15px;line-height:1.3;box-sizing:border-box}
.rxc-shell *{box-sizing:border-box;font-family:inherit;text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;font-size:inherit;line-height:inherit}
.rxc-shell a{color:inherit;text-decoration:none}
.rxc-shell a:hover{text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.3em}
.rxc-shell a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #2B3EFF;outline-offset:3px}
.rxc-shell .wrap{max-width:78rem;margin:0 auto;padding:.75rem clamp(1.25rem,4vw,4.5rem);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap}
.rxc-shell.top{border-bottom:2px solid var(--ink)}
.rxc-shell.bottom{border-top:1px solid var(--hair);font-size:14px;color:var(--quiet)}
.rxc-shell.bottom a{color:var(--ink)}
.rxc-shell .crumbs{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;color:var(--quiet);min-width:0}
.rxc-shell .crumbs a{font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem}
.rxc-shell .crumbs span.here{overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;white-space:nowrap}
.rxc-shell .status{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:.4rem;color:var(--quiet)}
.rxc-shell .status i{width:.5rem;height:.5rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--voice-b);display:inline-block}
.rxc-shell .btn{border:2px solid var(--ink);padding:.45rem .8rem;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;line-height:1;color:var(--ink)}
.rxc-shell .btn:hover{background:var(--ink);color:var(--paper);text-decoration:none}
.rxc-shell .right{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap}
.rxc-shell .btn{border-radius:0;background:transparent;display:inline-block}
.rxc-shell .btn:hover{transform:none}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="rxc-shell top" role="banner">
  <div class="wrap">
    <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="3" width="12" height="12"/><rect x="9" y="9" width="12" height="12"/></svg>RadicalxChange</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <a href="/projects/">Projects</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <span class="here">Warringah on migration</span>
    </nav>
    <div class="right">
      <span class="status"><i></i>Preliminary results, data to 6am AEDT, 18 November 2026</span>
      <a class="btn" href="mailto:info@radicalxchange.org?subject=Warringah%20migration%20results">Contact the team</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<header class="hero" id="top">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-text">
        <h1><span class="ln">Warringah wants</span><span class="ln"><span class="box">a long-term plan</span></span><span class="ln">for migration</span></h1>
        <p class="sub">People disagree about how many should come, and how fast. But most want migration planned years ahead, with homes, transport, schools and hospitals ready in time.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="btn solid" href="#groups">See what Warringah said</a><a class="btn line" href="#priorities">The changes people want most</a></div>
        <p class="turnout">Since 30 October 2026 · 452 people have taken part</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cards" role="list" aria-label="Two statements from the conversation, one from each group">
        <div class="card c1" role="listitem"><p class="who"><i aria-hidden="true"></i>Group 1 · Faster, fairer visas</p><q>The Government should invest in strong settlement supports to help everyone, regardless of their visa type</q></div>
        <div class="sticker" aria-hidden="true"><div><span>More than</span><b>4 in 5</b><span>in both groups want transport, schools and healthcare planned ahead</span></div></div>
        <div class="card c2" role="listitem"><p class="who"><i aria-hidden="true"></i>Group 2 · Fewer people, more slowly</p><q>Temporary Student Visa holders should have to leave the country and reapply for permanent migration if they want to return.</q></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<main>
<section class="glance" aria-label="At a glance">
  <div class="wrap glance-grid">
    <a class="gl" href="#groups">
      <h3>Two main groups</h3>
      <div class="split" aria-hidden="true"><i style="width:67%;background:var(--g1)"></i><i style="width:33%;background:var(--g2)"></i></div>
      <div class="split-n" aria-hidden="true"><span><i class="dot g1"></i>2 in 3</span><span>1 in 3<i class="dot g2"></i></span></div>
      <p>Two in three want faster, fairer visas. One in three want fewer people to come, more slowly.</p>
      <span class="more">See the groups</span>
    </a>
    <a class="gl dark" href="#agree">
      <h3>Both groups want a plan</h3>
      <p>Most people in both groups want migration planned years ahead, with homes, transport, schools and hospitals ready in time.</p>
      <span class="more">See where they agree</span>
    </a>
    <a class="gl tinted" href="#priorities">
      <h3>First choice: plan homes and services with migration</h3>
      <p>At a community session on 11 November, 46 of 53 people backed planning migration together with housing and infrastructure.</p>
      <span class="more">See the priorities</span>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block" id="groups" aria-labelledby="groups-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <h2 id="groups-h">Most people fit into one of two groups</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="groups-row">
      <div class="gcard one">
        <div class="gtop"><span class="big">2<small> in </small>3</span><span class="who"><b><i class="dot g1"></i>Group 1: Faster, fairer visas</b>245 people</span></div>
        <div class="qbox lead"><p class="lab">What sets them apart</p><q>I'd trust the system more if visa decisions were fast, because people's lives, jobs and families are on hold while they wait.</q>
          <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>80%</b> of Group 1 agree</span><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>28%</b> of Group 2</span></div></div>
        <div class="qbox"><q>No one should have to choose between staying in a bad job and losing their visa. Workers need to be able to walk away.</q>
          <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>82%</b> of Group 1 agree</span><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>35%</b> of Group 2</span></div></div>
        <div class="qbox"><q>I'd trust the system more if two people who apply on the same day weren't left waiting very different times, for reasons no one explains.</q>
          <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>78%</b> of Group 1 agree</span><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>37%</b> of Group 2</span></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="gcard two">
        <div class="gtop"><span class="big">1<small> in </small>3</span><span class="who"><b><i class="dot g2"></i>Group 2: Fewer people, more slowly</b>120 people</span></div>
        <div class="qbox lead"><p class="lab">What sets them apart</p><q>For me, trust comes down to the numbers: too many people have arrived too quickly for our communities to keep up.</q>
          <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>82%</b> of Group 2 agree</span><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>16%</b> of Group 1</span></div></div>
        <div class="qbox"><q>Temporary visas should stay temporary. People who come on them know the deal, and staying on shouldn't be expected.</q>
          <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>83%</b> of Group 2 agree</span><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>39%</b> of Group 1</span></div></div>
        <div class="qbox"><q>I'd rather the system took longer and got the checks right than rushed decisions.</q>
          <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>80%</b> of Group 2 agree</span><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>44%</b> of Group 1</span></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="small-note">The people who joined in aren’t a random sample, so these groups describe who took part, not all of Warringah. 87 people aren’t in a group: they voted on too few statements, or didn’t agree or disagree with any.</p>

    <div class="sub-head"><h3>Where everyone sits</h3></div>
    <div class="map-card" id="map-card">
      <p class="map-lead">Each dot is one person, placed by how they voted. People who voted alike sit close together, so the higher the pile, the more people voted that way.</p>
      <svg id="map" viewBox="0 0 1000 300" role="img" aria-labelledby="map-desc"><desc id="map-desc">365 people placed along the main divide in the votes. Group 1, Faster, fairer visas, 245 people, sits to the left in a high pile. Group 2, Fewer people, more slowly, 120 people, spreads out in a low pile to the right. A dashed line inside Group 2 marks where its 24 people furthest along begin.</desc></svg>
      <div class="map-foot">
        <button class="someone" type="button" id="someone">Show me someone</button>
      </div>
      <div class="person" id="person" aria-live="polite"></div>
      <p class="map-hint"><span class="h-fine">Hover over a dot to see how that person voted.</span><span class="h-touch">Tap the map or press “Show me someone” to see how one person voted.</span></p>
      <div class="st-key">
        <p class="st-h">The two groups, and a closer look inside Group 2</p>
        <ul class="st-list">
          <li class="grp"><p class="st-t"><i class="dot g1" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="st-n">Group 1: Faster, fairer visas</span><span class="st-c">245 people</span></p><p class="st-d">They want visa decisions made faster, rules that don’t change after you’ve applied, and the freedom to leave a bad job without losing your visa. There’s no clear split inside this group.</p></li>
          <li class="grp g2row"><p class="st-t"><i class="dot g2" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="st-n">Group 2: Fewer people, more slowly</span><span class="st-c">120 people</span></p></li>
          <li class="part"><p class="st-t"><span class="st-b" aria-hidden="true">A</span><span class="st-n">Fewer, but flexible</span><span class="st-c">96 people</span></p><p class="st-d">They want fewer people, more slowly, but most would still make room for care workers, genuine shortages and people who’ve built a life here. Most also say migration has made life here better.</p></li>
          <li class="part"><p class="st-t"><span class="st-b" aria-hidden="true">B</span><span class="st-n">Fewer, with firm limits</span><span class="st-c">24 people</span></p><p class="st-d">They want fewer people too, and most of them also oppose a visa for care workers, quicker sponsorship for genuine shortages, and a path to stay for long-term residents.</p></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block deep" id="agree" aria-labelledby="agree-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head side">
      <h2 id="agree-h">Even where they disagree, they agree on something</h2>
      <p class="head-line">At least 7 in 10 people in each group agreed with 38 statements. Here are five of them, each beside a related statement the two groups disagree on.</p>
    </div>
    <div id="pairs"></div>
    <details class="all">
      <summary>See all 38 statements both groups agreed with</summary>
      <ol class="all-list" id="all"></ol>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block tint" id="priorities" aria-labelledby="prio-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <h2 id="prio-h">The six changes people want most</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="how">
      <div class="costs" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="cost"><div class="sq s1"><i></i></div><p><b>1 vote</b><br>1 credit</p></div>
        <div class="cost"><div class="sq s4"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><p><b>2 votes</b><br>4 credits</p></div>
        <div class="cost"><div class="sq s9"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><p><b>3 votes</b><br>9 credits</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="cap">At a community session on 11 November, 53 people used quadratic voting to spread a budget of credits across 13 possible changes, for or against. Each extra vote on the same idea costs more, so the totals show what people care about most.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="finding">The top three match ideas most people in both groups agreed with in the conversation.</p>
    <div class="prio-grid" id="prio"></div>
    <div class="no-card">
      <div><h3>And one clear no</h3><p class="t">Prioritise migrants in high-paying jobs, using salary rather than shortage lists to decide who qualifies.</p><p class="s">30 people opposed it and 9 backed it. Most of the opposition was mild, with one or two votes each.</p></div>
      <div><div class="tally"><p class="big">−47<span>net votes</span></p></div></div>
    </div>
    <details class="rest">
      <summary>See the other six changes</summary>
      <ol class="rest-list" id="rest"></ol>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head"><h2 id="about-h">How this worked</h2></div>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li class="step"><span class="fig">36</span><h3>Starter statements</h3><p>The conversation opened with 36 statements for people to agree or disagree with.</p></li>
      <li class="step"><span class="fig">452</span><h3>People took part</h3><p>Since 30 October they have voted agree, disagree or pass, and added statements of their own.</p></li>
      <li class="step"><span class="fig">2</span><h3>Groups emerged</h3><p>Polis, an open-source tool, grouped people who voted alike. Nobody chose a group. We named them.</p></li>
      <li class="step"><span class="fig">53</span><h3>Voters set priorities</h3><p>On 11 November they spread a budget of credits across 13 possible changes, using quadratic voting.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <details class="fine">
      <summary>Notes for checking the numbers</summary>
      <div class="arows">
        <div class="arow"><h3>Reading the percentages</h3><p>Each figure is the share of a group who agreed, out of those in the group who voted on that statement. Later statements had fewer voters, so where fewer than 20 people in a group voted, we show how many.</p></div>
        <div class="arow"><h3>Reading the map</h3><p>We rebuilt the map from the published votes using the same method as Polis, so people sit close to where the Polis report places them, but not in exactly the same spots. Left to right is the main divide in the votes. Where many people sit close together, their dots pile up, so a dot can sit a little to one side of its exact place.</p><p>Each person’s card shows up to two of their votes as examples. For each group they sided with, it shows the statement most of that group agreed with, preferring statements the person agreed with over ones they rejected.</p></div>
        <div class="arow"><h3>A closer look inside Group 2</h3><p>Inside Group 2, views change sharply near the far end of the line. The 24 people furthest along differ from the other 96 on seven statements. On each, at least 65% agreed on one side and at most 35% on the other, with at least 21 people voting on each side, and a gap that big would happen by chance less than once in a thousand times.</p><p>A visa for care workers: 8% of the 24 agreed, against 69% of the 96. A real path to stay for long-term residents: 26% against 72%. Quick sponsorship for genuine shortages: 26% against 70%. Migration filling genuine worker shortages: 22% against 66%. Keeping migration levels flexible: 29% against 82%. “The food, festivals and friendships migration has brought…”: 0% against 75%. “A well-managed system means everyone feels safe…”: 17% against 73%.</p><p>When we shuffled the group’s order, no more than one statement ever split it this way, and both parts voted on a median of 53 statements. Inside Group 1 only one statement did, too few for a closer look. We also looked for unlikely allies, people in both groups who back the same statements, and found none that held up.</p></div>
        <div class="arow"><h3>The group cards</h3><p>Each card shows three statements most of the group agreed with and far fewer of the other group did. RadicalxChange chose which three to show. We chose statements about how the visa system should work.</p></div>
        <div class="arow"><h3>Who and what we counted</h3><p>155 statements were open for voting: the 36 starter statements, 46 added by the moderators during the conversation, and 73 written by residents. The moderators removed 331 others before anyone else voted on them.</p><p>We count the 452 people who voted on at least one of those 155 statements. Between them they cast 23,944 votes. Polis’s own count of 468 also includes 16 accounts whose only votes were on statements they wrote themselves.</p><p>3 people voted on enough statements to be placed in a group, but didn’t agree or disagree with any of them: every vote they cast was a pass. They count as taking part, but we haven’t placed them in a group, because a pass doesn’t show where someone stands. Polis places them anyway, because it reads a pass as halfway between agree and disagree.</p></div>
        <div class="arow"><h3>Pairing the statements</h3><p>RadicalxChange chose which statements to pair. Every number comes straight from the results.</p></div>
        <div class="arow"><h3>The priority vote</h3><p>A separate vote with its own voters. We set aside ballots that used fewer than 10 credits and kept the fuller ballot where someone voted twice, leaving 53 voters. Net votes are votes for minus votes against. The matching statements from the conversation are close in meaning, not identical in wording.</p><p>The chart shared after the session shows 56 voters, because it keeps two ballots that used 6 and 7 credits and counts two names that differ only in capital letters as two people. The order of all 13 changes is the same either way.</p></div>
        <div class="arow"><h3>The data</h3><p>From the Polis export of 18 November 2026, 6am AEDT. The conversation is still open, so these results are preliminary. Statements appear exactly as people wrote them.</p></div>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>
