ewcomers and the wider community.","232":"A fairer and more affordable partner visa system would increase confidence in Australia’s migration system.","238":"Australia’s family law and child support systems should better recognise the circumstances of migrant families.","257":"Family migration can provide childcare and support that helps families participate in the workforce.","260":"Lower migration would reduce some of the pressure on rents and housing demand.","261":"Government should help fund the recognition of migrants’ overseas qualifications so their skills are not wasted.","307":"There should be a watchdog to monitor discrimination & racism against migrants","310":"The Government should invest in strong settlement supports to help everyone, regardless of their visa type","323":"all visas, regardless of category should always be viewed through a DV Prevention and Gender Equality lens in addition to other criteria","325":"The soft diplomacy benefits arising from international students studying in Australia should be widely promoted.","338":"Community sponsorship of refugees should be counted as additional to the government's own humanitarian commitments.","343":"The current path of allowing student visa holders to work and then be sponsored is good for the Australian economy and culture.","344":"familyreunion  visas are just as important as other visas in particular for residents /citizens who have been contributing to our nation","375":"Government should adopt, fund and implement the National Anti-Racism Framework. Introduce a positive duty to prevent racial discrimination"},"nsplit":22}</script>
